  "2026-10-22T20:56:43.333Z",codex-agent,"Legacy identity compatibility added after the first restored PM run passed 43/43 (351.45 seconds). An existing acknowledgement without bindings can now add explicit SDK bindings only when all acknowledged field values are unchanged after canonicalization. Local edits survive, missing items and changed baseline values refuse, writer-lock revision changes refuse, failed migration restores the original base, and a later source revision is preserved with recovery_required. Two real-tracker migration regressions passed 2/2. Reverting only acknowledgeBeadsSnapshot to its pre-round function failed both (2/2) with base_exists instead of supporting safe migration. Exact proof command: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"legacy source bindings\" test/reconcile.test.ts. This brings independent revert experiments to 11 expected regression failures; all source restored. The same command is registered on the item for the final PM runner check. Whole-PR self-review also verifies source identity scans ignore ordinary saved review-plan JSON files and retain bindings when a bound core item disappears."
  "2026-10-22T21:14:30.968Z",codex-agent,"First full npm release gate ran 399/399 tests successfully with zero failures/skips (704.14 seconds), but correctly refused the unchanged 100% branch threshold: reconcile.ts was 99.74% branches, aggregate 99.93%. The only gap was the legacy no-bindings fallback in applyBeadsReconciliation. Strengthened the existing raw legacy-base convergence/rollback fixture to omit bindings, matching the historical schema; no source implementation or threshold change was needed. Its fixed regression passed 1/1 and exercised the missing branch. Repeated the classifier-only revert against this stronger fixture: 1/1 failed, then restored the source. The earlier 11 independent revert failures still cover the same behaviors; this is a repeat of the legacy comparison proof. Full npm gate will be rerun before Bun. This was a coverage failure, not a timeout."
  "2026-10-22T21:36:39.802Z",codex-agent,"Final validation: isolated env HOME=\"$(mktemp -d)\" GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check passed 399/399, zero failures/skips, all nine source files at 100% lines/branches/functions; test phase 696.63 seconds. Equivalent bun run release:check passed 399/399, zero failures/skips, identical 100% coverage; test phase 324.69 seconds. Both documented 77/77 declarations and found zero production vulnerabilities; workflow, build, package dry-run, changelog and release provenance/date contracts passed. No timeout occurred. The first npm attempt passed 399 tests but missed one legacy no-bindings branch; the strengthened regression closed it and the full rerun passed without threshold changes. All 45 reconciliation/compiled CLI cases are included in each final gate. PM-linked checks passed 43 tests before the legacy-binding extension and 2 migration tests afterward; the added missing-base compensation branch also passed targeted coverage. Public-copy validation passed 93 baseline items plus RAW type/deadline follow-up, source unchanged. Final prescribed GraphQL query (comments first 20, no omitted pages) succeeded: zero unresolved threads. Latest CodeRabbit review body is empty; no outside-diff findings. No review replies/resolutions by this agent. Source, tests, README/example and all tracker evidence will be committed together; dist rebuilt and untracked by repository policy. Remaining constraints: pause ordinary writers during apply/compensation; whole-tracker invalidation remains conservative (pm-beads-51fi and pm-beads-qwvf stay open). Existing installer/fence drift pm-beads-v9r1 is unchanged. No dependency pins changed and no PR merge or package release."
